Z||000000||varnster||06-27-2001||09:43 PM||||I pulled the master cylinder, and the booster<BR>to paint and clean underneath, do you guys recomend rebuilding this unit{MASTER} while its out?<BR>its performing fine, the car has 106,000 miles on the OD, thanks!||||reg||5
Z||000001||PBJ||06-27-2001||11:34 PM||||In my opinion car will break enough that you just fix what is broken.  Rebuilding a master cylinder if it is working fine goes beyond preventative maint.  But.....||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||06-28-2001||12:23 AM||||Basically, if it was working, WHY the H_ll are you fooling with it? These cars don't have enough brake problems?<P>The master cyl is more complicated than most people think. read my brake articles for more detail. If you really feel you should do something to it then just get a rebuilt one from one of the many normal outlets. <P>Rebuilding an MC isn't rocket science but it's not for amatures either. Honing a cylinder properly is allot harder than the various books/articles often make it out. <P>You have to hone 3 diferant bores.<BR>Each has to be perfect.<P>failure in any one of them can result in the cylinder failing very sudenly. A screw up may not manifest for days or weeks after the job.||||reg||1
Z||000003||varnster||06-28-2001||09:08 AM||||jesus, man I was just asking?, I was just <BR>talking about the soft goods not honing<BR>the walls, thanks, I'll just leave good enough alone.||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||06-28-2001||01:22 PM||||the famous words once again for new people...IF IT AINT BROKE - DONT FIX IT !! and as someone added 'fix it till its broke'.||||reg||1
